{"id":"project-LICHEN-ow1e.148","title":"lichen-node DispatchError::PayloadTooShort should use lichen_core::error::TooShort","description":"lichen-node/src/port_dispatch.rs defines:
  pub enum DispatchError {
      UnknownPort(u16),
      PayloadTooShort,  // unit variant
      ReservedPort,
  }

PayloadTooShort is semantically identical to lichen_core::error::TooShort but doesn't wrap it or carry the expected/actual size information.

Compare to lichen-coap which wraps the shared type:
  pub enum CoapError {
      TooShort(TooShort),  // wraps with diagnostic info
      ...
  }

What goes wrong: When dispatch fails due to payload being too short, callers cannot determine how many bytes were expected vs received. Error handling code cannot use a unified pattern across DispatchError and other protocol errors.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"me@mark.atwood.name","created_at":"2026-07-06T15:38:15.040514Z","created_by":"Mark Atwood","updated_at":"2026-07-06T17:45:13.807406Z","closed_at":"2026-07-06T17:45:13.807406Z","close_reason":"Closed","labels":["error-type","owner-reserved","review","workspace-api"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"project-LICHEN-ow1e.148","depends_on_id":"project-LICHEN-ow1e","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-06T15:38:15.041042Z"}]}

